{"name":"Basket of Bobbins","hex":"#c8c0b8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"basket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight woven container, generally round, open at the top, and tapering toward the bottom.","A bed for a cat."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a basket or baskets.","To cross-collateralize the royalty advances for multiple works so that the creator is not paid until all of those works have achieved a certain level of success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/basket"},{"term":"bobbins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bobbin"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["crap, rubbish, something worthless or nonsensical"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bobbins"}],"entries":[{"title":"Basket","blocks":[{"text":"A basket is a container that is traditionally constructed from stiff fibers, and can be made from a range of materials, including wood splints, runners, and cane. While most baskets are made from plant materials, other materials such as horsehair, baleen, or metal wire can be used. Baskets are generally woven by hand. Some baskets are fitted with a lid, while others are left open on top."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Baskets_in_Haikou_03.jpg/330px-Baskets_in_Haikou_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basket","wikidata":"Q201097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Tressage_du_panier.jpg/500px-Tressage_du_panier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Tressage_du_panier.jpg/1280px-Tressage_du_panier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Tressage_du_panier.jpg/500px-Tressage_du_panier.jpg?utm_so